// THE SURGE — HIGH VOLTAGE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// THE SURGE as euphoric hard trance — HIGH VOLTAGE. One of four Surge versions; a game
// alternate of surge, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk.
// Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// 150 BPM, A minor, a whole step up (B minor) for the climax. Trance, not hard-dance:
// a psy ROLLING bass — kick, bass, bass, bass on every beat — on the Surge's own roots
// (A1 F1 | G1 E2, as surge.js plays them), trance-gated supersaw chords (a sixteenth gate
// into a quarter pump), the riff on a supersaw and a screamer with a plain square under it,
// a long piano breakdown, and the half-speed THEME as a mega-saw anthem with the riff an
// octave up around it. The Surge break (x.xx.xx.x.xx.xx.) plays on the kick in bars 1–2,
// then moves to a 909 rim over four on the floor and stays there all song, so the break
// survives the kick. The Surge clap (....x..x....x...) keeps its extra hit in drop one
// and the finale.
// 
//   1–4    IGNITION — the original loop: the riff through a filter opening bar by bar,
//          the break on the kick, the Surge bass line; bar 3 four-on-the-floor, the
//          break moves to the rim, the bass rolls, the gated saws enter; bar 4 the
//          screamer and the crystal 8va join (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    build — the riff on a crystal pluck, gated saws opening 600 Hz → 5 kHz,
//          snare quarters → sixteenths, riser, an empty last beat
//   9–24   DROP ONE — the riff on supersaw + screamer + square; 17–24 the THEME on the
//          pluck under it (the riff against itself at half speed), richer chords,
//          the octave-pop roll; bar 24 the riff's head buffer-repeats, crushed
//   25–40  CHANNEL SURF — four windows, each a hook on its cabinet's timbre over the
//          Surge's roots and the trance groove, each cut out by a glitch that brings
//          the riff back: 28 buffer-repeat + bit-crush, 32 tape sag + the riff's answer
//          clean, 36 a one-beat hole + a crushed stutter, 40 a tape-stop power-down
//   41–56  BREAKDOWN — drums out; the electric grand plays four hooks over the Surge's
//          chords, strings under, choir from 43, sub from 45; then the THEME on the
//          grand (51–54) with the roll starting under it (53); at 55 the riff returns
//          at full speed a whole step up, filters opening, riser, empty last beat
//   57–72  DROP TWO — B minor: the THEME on the mega-saw + square, the riff an octave
//          up around it, choir, crash every four; 65–72 the grand doubles the THEME in
//          octaves and the screamer joins the riff; bar 72 is home already (B minor's
//          G is A minor's G, and its E leads into 73)
//   73–80  EVERYTHING AT ONCE — A minor: riff 8va + THEME + CARDBOARD on the toy piano;
//          from 77 SPEED's riff hockets on the screamer and the grand doubles the THEME
//   81–84  the riff at home pitch (81), crushed stutter (82), 32nd-gated saws + riser +
//          roll (83), a tape stop on the riff and an empty beat (84) — into the loop
// 
// THE QUOTES — all eight, each at its own pitch (every hook is already in the Surge's key):
//   SPEED ZONE           25–28  screamer + square (speed's A gear), and 77–80 in the finale
//   TERMINAL VELOCITY    29–32  alloy chime + crystal 8va (the day figure)
//   RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY    33–36  square + toy piano (the Popcorn hook)
//   FIELD SERVICE        37–40  electric grand in octaves + square (A then B phrase)
//   CRYPT SHIFT          41–44  grand in octaves, strings, choir (A–C–B … G# B G#)
//   FROST FORTRESS       45–46  grand, over Dm and F
//   CARDBOARD KINGDOM    47–48  grand; and 73–80 on the toy piano over the riff
//   CORPORATE KOMBAT     49–50  grand, over G–Em and F–E
// The riff or the THEME plays in every section except inside a window, and the riff
// comes back in every cut between windows.
// 
// LOOP: the cabinet screen loops bars 1–4 (IGNITION). The song loops bars 9–84
// (121.6 s of 134.4 s), so a clean run of the Surge (about 120 s) rarely hears
// the loop point; bars 83–84 build back into drop one exactly as 7–8 do.
// 
// 84 bars at 150. Written by work/local/_surge-remix-high-voltage.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs and work/local/_surge-quotes.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-surge.mjs — re-run it after a regeneration): the
// glitches are real now, on the master. Buffer repeats (the whole mix) at 8, 24, 28, 36, 56, 82;
// true holes — every lane cut, the master to -48 dB — on 8 and 56 beat 4, 36 beat 3, 84 beat 4;
// tape stops as a lowpass closing a sixteenth at a time on 32, 40 and 84. No TAPE snapshots.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
